# [[ title .Name ]]

A [Quanarch](https://quanarch.org) project.

```
[[ .Name ]]/
├── packages/
│   └── [[ (index .Quas 0).Name ]]/
├── quanar/
└── quans/
    └── [[ (index .Quans 0).Name ]]/
```

- `packages/[[ (index .Quas 0).Name ]]`: the qua, the contract between the quanar and its quans
- `quanar`: loads the quans and plugs in the qua
- `quans/[[ (index .Quans 0).Name ]]`: a quan, business logic loaded by the quanar

## Run

In two terminals:

```sh
# builds the quan and serves it on port [[ (index .Quans 0).Port ]]
cd quans/[[ (index .Quans 0).Name ]] && npm run watch

# starts the quanar on port 5173
cd quanar && npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:5173/[[ (index .Quans 0).Name ]]

The counter on the page belongs to the quan, but the quan never adds to it
itself: it calls `increment` on the qua, and the quanar does the counting.
